# Generated by matugen — DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
#
# The one colour the whole rice is derived from.
#
# matugen extracts a source colour from the wallpaper and builds a Material You
# scheme around it. The lock screen consumes that scheme directly (the two
# hyprlock templates beside this one). Everything else — the shell, kitty, GTK,
# rofi, the login screen — takes the Catppuccin flavour's own ramp and re-tints
# it toward this hue, which keeps each slot's lightness and so keeps text
# readable whatever the wallpaper turns out to be. See apollo-settings/dynamic.go.
#
# It is staged in the cache rather than written straight to those files because
# matugen renders its templates unconditionally, on every wallpaper change,
# while the fan-out only happens when dynamic colours are switched on. Staging
# is what makes the toggle possible without a second matugen config.
APOLLO_SOURCE="#{{colors.primary.default.hex_stripped}}"
